// Redacted[T] is a secret: a value of T that no text form shows (docs/
// spec/stdlib.md, config). Effect's Redacted has the same purpose: keep a
// token or a password out of logs, error reports and encoded output. Ergo
// gets it by construction where Effect checks it at run time:
//
//   - Redacted is an operation type, so it has no text form: "\(r)" of a
//     value whose type reaches it is refused by the checker (S108), and an
//     error report writes the field as <Redacted>, the type's name, never
//     the value (types.md, Methods 6; lower TestRedactedNeverPrints).
//   - It has no wire form (types.md, Codecs 1: an operation type), so
//     encode, json.Encode and toml.Encode of a value that reaches it are
//     refused at check time. A program that must write a secret gives the
//     codec itself: its own type with a by-name pair whose Wire calls
//     Reveal, in its own package, where a reader sees it.
//   - A law's counterexample writes it as the call of its builder,
//     config.NewRedacted[T](…), never the value.
//   - Its Go body keeps the value behind a pointer field, never inline, so
//     Go's fmt can print at most an address, and its String, GoString,
//     Format, MarshalJSON, MarshalText and LogValue are "<redacted>": Go
//     code that reaches the value through a foreign call or a defect's
//     text prints no byte of it (runtime/v1 TestRedactedNeverRenders).
//
// Reveal is the one read of the value. It is sealed (check.SealedStd):
// NewRedacted, an extern, returns it, so no program value implements it.
//
// law-exempt: its one operation gives back the value NewRedacted was given; the top-level law RevealIsTheValue states it over NewRedacted, the only provider, and needs a comparable T.
type Redacted[T] {
	runtimeOnly(),
	// Reveal is the value the secret holds.
	Reveal() T,
}

// NewRedacted is a secret that holds v.
extern go ergo.local/prototype/runtime/v1.NewRedacted func NewRedacted[T](v T) Redacted[T]

// RevealIsTheValue: a secret gives back the value it was made with.
law RevealIsTheValue(v string, n int) {
	NewRedacted(v).Reveal() == v && NewRedacted(n).Reveal() == n
}
